course: dictionary
lesson: 14891
title: Formal words and what they mean
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Some words belong to careful, formal writing, such as letters, rules and exam texts. «Recompense» is one of them. It is about fairness: when someone has been harmed, lost something or taken trouble, recompense is what they receive to put things right.
explain: «The shop gave Mia a new coat in recompense for the one that was torn at the till.» Here recompense is something given to make up for a loss. In everyday speech people say "compensation" or "payback", so you can test your meaning by swapping one of those words into the sentence and checking that it still makes sense.
explain: Recompense can also mean a reward for work or effort. «The farmer gave the boys coins as recompense for their hard work.» As a verb, to recompense someone means to pay or reward them: «The town recompensed the families for the flood damage.»
fact: Recompense is a formal word, so you will mostly find it in letters, law and exam texts.
fact: As a noun, recompense means money or something else given to make up for harm, loss, trouble or work.
fact: Useful phrases are «in recompense for», «as recompense» and «without recompense».
fact: In everyday English, people usually say «compensation», «payback» or «pay» instead of recompense.
fact: As a noun, recompense is uncountable, so we say «some recompense», not «two recompenses».
exercise: «The company paid the workers extra money in recompense for their long hours.» What does recompense mean here? | *Money given to make up for the hard work | A list of rules for the workplace | A letter asking for a day off | A punishment for being late
exercise: Which everyday word could replace recompense in «The insurance company paid us money as recompense for the flood damage»? | Rubbish | Holiday | *Compensation | Lunch
exercise: «The club recompensed the referee for his trouble.» What does recompensed mean? | Gave him a yellow card | Forgot about him after the match | Sent him home early | *Paid him to make up for his trouble
test: «The lost dog was found, and its owner gave the finder a reward as recompense.» What is the recompense in this sentence? | A warning to be more careful | *A reward given to repay the finder for their effort | A lost ticket | A kind of dog
test: Fill the gap: «He received a medal ___ his bravery.» | in recompense of | in recompensed for | recompense him for | *in recompense for
exam: Which sentence uses recompense correctly? | *She was paid a small sum in recompense for her lost time. | The dog recompense happily in the garden. | We recompensed to the park after lunch. | The recompense was a sunny day and a cold drink.
